---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Legal" description="NOVAHODOS legal, privacy, consent, and use boundaries." lang="en">
  <section class="section hero compact-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Legal</p><h1>Clear boundaries build trust.</h1><p class="lede">These pages define public-safe use boundaries for AMI. They may be updated as formal legal review continues.</p></section>
  <section class="section stack">
    <article id="terms" class="card"><p class="eyebrow">Terms</p><h2>Terms of Use</h2><p>AMI is a metabolic navigation and personal optimization tool. It supports wellness-oriented decision making and does not replace professional medical care.</p><p>Use AMI as personal decision support, not as a clinical order, diagnosis, treatment plan, or emergency service.</p></article>
    <article id="privacy" class="card"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p><h2>Privacy Policy</h2><p>AMI may process profile, fasting, labs you enter, daily signals, and sync state for personal metabolic navigation. We do not sell your data to third parties.</p><p>Full policy, retention, and account deletion instructions: <a class="email-link" href="/privacy">/privacy</a> (includes <a class="email-link" href="/privacy#delete-account">#delete-account</a>).</p></article>
    <article id="use-boundaries" class="card highlight"><p class="eyebrow">Responsible Use</p><h2>AMI supports metabolic navigation within wellness boundaries.</h2><p>AMI organizes metrics, trajectory, and context to guide clearer daily decisions. It does not diagnose, prevent, treat, cure, or mitigate disease.</p><p>Navigation supports daily fasting decisions. Precision Calibration adds lab-informed context when available, but abnormal results should be reviewed with a qualified healthcare professional.</p></article>
    <article id="health-disclaimer" class="card"><p class="eyebrow">Health Disclaimer</p><h2>AMI does not replace medical care.</h2><p>If you have significant symptoms, pregnancy, diagnosed disease, active medication, hypoglycemia risk, or clinical concerns, consult a qualified healthcare professional before using AMI or changing fasting behavior.</p><p>Break the fast and seek medical guidance if persistent dizziness, palpitations, confusion, pain, hypoglycemia, or deterioration appear.</p></article>
    <article id="data-consent" class="card"><p class="eyebrow">Data Consent</p><h2>Consent must be explicit.</h2><p>Data collection, storage, restoration, and deletion must be explained clearly. Plan access controls features; it does not define ownership of the user's history.</p></article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>